{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3db","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aba0-ed5d-7bd3-a9ee-56e3c44bc574"},"sequence":72,"recorded_at":1780531400000139,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"828a2271-c160-41d3-ae7c-b2b4f5a16018","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"828a2271-c160-41d3-ae7c-b2b4f5a16018","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"828a2271-c160-41d3-ae7c-b2b4f5a16018"},"call_id":"call_01a0aba1324e74b1882449987de23d4d","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-cr9.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 9 of TASK-260830-21gygk (story_final, base 8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653, candidate tree 6eb65f537f4ebffe6e6044f5b64ffc1b89d4487e, published by RUN-260910-c835df). This is the review of the rework that answered the CR8 verdict; the producer outcome is named TASK-260830-21gygk_results-rev8.md and the matrix TASK-260830-21gygk_conformance-matrix-rev8.md — the numbering differs from the CR revision on purpose. Read the CR8 verdict and review-evidence bundle, the producer outcome, the conformance matrix, the rev9 patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. Superseded briefs named reviewer-after-rev8 and earlier are historical; this brief governs.\n2|\n3|Reproduce TestRev8CheckpointProfileAuthority on the exact candidate: the four valid creation-profile/null controls and the missing profile.changed reference negatives across direct/task_board persistence and winner/necessary-ancestor checkpoints, through BuildPlan, fresh and old-plan Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus and AuthoritativeList. Then review the complete assigned C6 consumption semantics against pinned Section 5.4 and the referenced 2.4/5.2 using actual canonical payload, Session Record and closure inputs: valid subsequent profile.changed references; missing, non-newest, losing-lease and other wrong-authority references; historical, branching and lagging controls; old-plan authority substitution. New tests alone do not prove completeness: inspect the shared production owner checkCheckpointProfileAuthority and every callsite. Future materialization APIs are not delegation; canonical shape, digest or lease tuple are not profile-source semantics. Preserve the accepted CLI/publication/storage/transport/effects boundary without narrowing the consumer contract.\n4|\n5|Two accounting caveats you must resolve explicitly. First, N-checkpoint-heads is now killed by an error-class pin while the profile backstop still refuses the weakened-heads fixture: that proves refusal order and label precision, not semantic admission narrowing of the heads gate. Classify every one of the claimed 59 kills as semantic admission, label/class precision, or fixture failure; do not accept a blanket 59-narrowing figure, and do not reopen product behavior that CR7/CR8 already established unless evidence contradicts it. Second, the producer's pipeline shape `python | tail; echo $?` reports tail's status; verify every claimed exit code from the raw logs or by re-running the instrument on the exact candidate, and prove the harmless SURVIVED control was actually applied through the same harness. Compile failures, unapplied plants and empty selections are not behavioral proof.\n6|\n7|The producer excludes from matrix C6b: fork.created provenance, resume checkpoint-ID existence, task-board launch lease-repeat/mode binding, change-source continuity, and confirmation gating. Decide whether each exclusion matches the originally scoped normative consumer contract for this leaf or narrows it; passing tests never justify scope narrowing, and a genuine caller-owned boundary must be named with its owning clause.\n8|\n9|Retain the closed findings unless new evidence contradicts them: CR7 missing/later checkpoint heads and old-plan substitution; direct/task_board persistence variants; necessary ancestry/creator; canonical lease identity; lagging copies; parked required source; the seven capabilities; predecessor/reducer/enums/creation crashes. The repeated finding family was canonical-shape versus actual cross-record authority; check that the shared owner enforces authority, not shape. Re-derive the 8-row AC accounting and the precise public-caller bounds from the source, not from the outcome prose.\n10|\n11|Method: review exact immutable CR bytes with isolated probes (throwaway clone or extracted tree), never mutate the live Story worktree, its index, branch or HEAD, and make no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration. Use the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill; all CI is local; reuse valid earlier evidence only with precise provenance. Attach the verdict as TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev9.md and reproducible evidence as TASK-260830-21gygk_review-evidence-rev9.tar.gz, complete the live merged checklist, then either accept_cr(TASK-260830-21gygk, revision=9, evidence=TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev9.md) or hand off changes requested with each finding classified P1/P2 and repeat-of named. Model: codex gpt-6-astra low. Canonical CLI: /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
